# _redirects
# Strategic Lab Partners content subdomain — SEO canonicalization / redirect rules
# Primary host: https://content.strategiclabpartners.com
#
# Contact destination: all recommended contact / email CTA links terminate at
#   mailto:orders@strategiclabpartners.com
#
# NOTE: Netlify _redirects cannot set title tags, meta descriptions, canonical
# tags, schema, or body copy. Those per-page SEO fields are implemented in the
# page templates / HTML head (see the SEO directive documented alongside this
# deploy). This file only carries the redirect rules needed to eliminate
# duplicate URLs and canonicalize the content subdomain.
#
# Canonical form for every page: NO trailing slash, NO .html extension.
# Netlify serves /faqs/<slug> directly from /faqs/<slug>.html (pretty URLs).

# --- GLOBAL CANONICALIZATION / CLEANUP -------------------------------------

# Legacy apostrophe (U+2019) variants of the innovation FAQ -> clean slug.
# These are genuine cross-URL redirects and 301 as expected.
/faqs/what-is-slp’s-approach-to-innovation.html            /faqs/what-is-slps-approach-to-innovation   301
/faqs/what-is-slp%E2%80%99s-approach-to-innovation.html    /faqs/what-is-slps-approach-to-innovation   301

# --- Trailing-slash duplicates: handled at the source, NOT via redirects ----
#
# The following FAQ pages previously existed as /faqs/<slug>/index.html, which
# produced duplicate trailing-slash URLs:
#   what-is-slp-connect, how-does-slp-connect-support-program-visibility,
#   decentralized-at-home-collections,
#   how-medical-fulfillment-improves-accuracy-and-reliability,
#   how-medical-fulfillment-supports-distributed-healthcare-networks,
#   how-medical-kitting-supports-multi-site-healthcare-organizations,
#   sample-integrity-genomics-transcriptomics-proteomics-metabolomics,
#   why-standardized-kits-are-important-for-healthcare-providers,
#   why-standardized-logistics-are-essential-for-medical-programs
#
# They have been flattened to /faqs/<slug>.html and their canonical tags,
# internal links, and sitemap entries now use the clean /faqs/<slug> form.
#
# A "/faqs/<slug>/  /faqs/<slug>  301" rule is intentionally NOT added:
# Netlify treats a trailing-slash path and its non-slash form as the SAME URL
# in redirect matching, so such a rule redirects the clean URL to itself and
# creates an infinite 301 loop. Slash consolidation is instead handled by the
# per-page rel="canonical" tag, which points at the non-trailing-slash URL.

# --- ASSET FILENAME CANONICALIZATION ---------------------------------------
#
# The SLP CONNECT white wordmark was originally published with spaces in its
# filename ("25 SLP Connect newlogo-white.png"). It is now stored without
# spaces, so the encoded legacy URL is redirected to the canonical file.
# The rule is written %20-encoded because _redirects is whitespace-delimited
# and a literal space would break rule parsing.
/assets/images/25%20SLP%20Connect%20newlogo-white.png   /assets/images/25-slp-connect-logo-white.png   301
